-- title:
--   Places of X₁(M) in characteristic p give chart points
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K'$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField M)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L$-Laurent series generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC ℚ M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) of $\Gamma_1(M)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, with $L$ as its fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K'$ compatible with $A \to L \to K'$. Let $j' \in K'$ be nonzero with Laurent series the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under the coefficient map to $L$. Let $\Omega_0$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ which is an $A$-algebra, and let $\bar{j}$ be an element of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC Ω₀ M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) whose Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqModC Ω₀`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15). Then there is an injective map $\Phi$ from the set of those places $v$ of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC Ω₀ M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) over $\Omega_0$ — a place being a valuation subring, distinct from the whole field, containing the image of $\Omega_0$ and a principal ideal ring — for which $\bar{j}$ lies in the valuation subring of $v$, to the set of $\Omega_0$-algebra homomorphisms $\Omega_0 \otimes_A \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K'\,j' \to \Omega_0$, where $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K'\,j'$ is the $A$-subalgebra of $K'$ of elements integral over $A[j']$, such that for every such $v$ the homomorphism $\Phi(v)$ sends $1 \otimes j'$ to the value `evalAt` of $\bar{j}$ at $v$, i.e. the preimage in $\Omega_0$ of the residue of $\bar{j}$ in the residue field of $v$.
--
--   This is the point-theoretic form of good reduction of $X_1(M)$ at primes $p \nmid M$: the places of the characteristic-$p$ $q$-expansion function field at which the reduced $j$-invariant is regular are realised injectively as $\Omega_0$-valued points of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}(\Omega_0 \otimes_A \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K'\,j')$ of the two-chart integral model, compatibly with the value of $j$. It is used in the study of the special fibre of that model, namely by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_injective_not_isRegularLocalRing_stalk_specialFibre_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_injective_not_isRegularLocalRing_stalk_specialFibre_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul).
